---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SourceList from '../components/SourceList.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const redFlags = await getCollection('redFlags');
const sourceRefs = [
  ...new Map(
    redFlags.flatMap((f) => f.data.sources).map((ref) => [ref.id, ref]),
  ).values(),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="When to see a clinician"
  description="Signs that a knee needs assessment rather than exercise."
>
  <h1>When to stop and see a clinician</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Most stiff knees are safe to move gently. These are the signs that mean something else may
    be going on, and that a clinician should look at the knee before you start working on it.
  </p>

  <div class="danger-list">
    <h3>See someone if any of these apply</h3>
    <ul>
      {redFlags.map((flag) => (
        <li><strong>{flag.data.sign}.</strong> {flag.data.description}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Why this list exists</h2>
    <p>
      Stiffness from tight muscles, an unused range, or arthritic change generally responds well
      to being moved. The signs above point to different situations — a mechanical block, an
      inflamed or infected joint, an acute injury — where moving the knee is not the right first
      step and may make things worse.
    </p>
    <p>
      None of that means a knee with one of these signs is necessarily serious. It means the
      question cannot be answered by a website, and someone should examine it.
    </p>

    <h2>Also worth remembering</h2>
    <p>
      If you have had knee surgery, your surgeon or physiotherapist may have set specific limits
      on how far to bend or straighten it. Those instructions are based on your knee and your
      procedure. Where anything here conflicts with them, follow the instructions you were given.
    </p>
    <p>
      And if something here is making your knee consistently worse rather than better, that is
      reason enough to stop and ask someone, whether or not it appears on the list above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <SourceList refs={sourceRefs} />
</BaseLayout>
